From: X2 bring-up <x2@local>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/a5xx: reset GPU at the start of hw_init

The bootloader can leave the GPU powered and its CP running before the
kernel takes over. On this platform the GX power domain is tied to the
SMMU, so runtime resume may not switch it off. In that case
a5xx_hw_init() rewinds the ringbuffer and writes CP_ME_INIT at offset 0
while the CP still holds its old read pointer, and the first
CP_ME_INIT wait times out with rptr/wptr = 0/C.

Reset RBBM unconditionally at the start of a5xx_hw_init() so the CP and
all GPU blocks start from a known state regardless of whether the
runtime resume callback ran.

Signed-off-by: X2 bring-up <x2@local>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a5xx_gpu.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a5xx_gpu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a5xx_gpu.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a5xx_gpu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a5xx_gpu.c
@@ -696,9 +696,20 @@ static int a5xx_hw_init(struct msm_gpu *gpu)
 {
 	struct adreno_gpu *adreno_gpu = to_adreno_gpu(gpu);
 	struct a5xx_gpu *a5xx_gpu = to_a5xx_gpu(adreno_gpu);
 	u32 hbb;
 	int ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * The GPU may still be powered and running from the bootloader, or
+	 * GX may follow the SMMU power domain. Reset RBBM here rather than
+	 * only in pm_resume(), because pm_runtime_get_sync() does not
+	 * necessarily invoke the runtime resume callback when the device is
+	 * already marked active.
+	 */
+	gpu_write(gpu, REG_A5XX_RBBM_SW_RESET_CMD, 1);
+	gpu_read(gpu, REG_A5XX_RBBM_SW_RESET_CMD);
+	gpu_write(gpu, REG_A5XX_RBBM_SW_RESET_CMD, 0);
+
 	gpu_write(gpu, REG_A5XX_VBIF_ROUND_ROBIN_QOS_ARB, 0x00000003);
 
 	if (adreno_is_a509(adreno_gpu) || adreno_is_a512(adreno_gpu) ||
